MISSION: COMPLETE END-TO-END VERIFICATION, REPAIR, AND PRODUCTION READINESS

You are the senior full-stack engineer, frontend architect, QA engineer, integration engineer, and deployment verification specialist responsible for the Choice real-estate platform.

Your task is to thoroughly audit, test, repair, integrate, and verify the entire existing application so that every page, route, redirect, button, form, modal, component, API request, database operation, property workflow, and user-facing feature works correctly from beginning to end.

This is an existing-project completion and verification task, not a request to create a superficial demo, redesign only the homepage, or produce a report without fixing problems.

Repository:
https://github.com/choice121/Choice

Work with the actual repository, current branch, existing architecture, configured integrations, and current implementation. Do not assume the project uses a particular framework or that previous changes are correct merely because they were merged or deployed.

1. PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Establish that the complete application works as one connected product.

The final result must satisfy all of the following:

* Every intended frontend page renders correctly.
* Every intended route resolves to the correct page.
* Every redirect works and preserves the correct destination and required state.
* No internal navigation leads to a blank screen, broken page, incorrect route, or unintended external destination.
* Every visible interactive control performs its intended action.
* Every form validates input, submits correctly, handles errors, and displays its resulting state.
* Every frontend-to-backend connection calls the correct endpoint with the correct data.
* Every database-dependent page retrieves and displays the correct data.
* Every supported create, read, update, and delete operation behaves correctly, with appropriate authorization and safeguards.
* Authentication, sessions, permissions, and protected routes work consistently.
* Property imports, source capture, validation, enrichment, AI description rewriting, review, approval, and publishing work through their intended end-to-end workflows.
* Loading, success, empty, error, and retry states are implemented and understandable.
* The interface displays actual application data rather than placeholder content when real data is expected.
* The production build runs the same intended implementation that was verified locally.
* Deployment, caching, environment configuration, and routing do not cause the live website to display stale or incomplete changes.
* All fixes are tested and supported by concrete evidence.

A successful build is not proof that the application works. A page rendering is not proof that its controls work. An API returning a response is not proof that the result reaches the frontend correctly. A successful deployment is not proof that the deployed application contains the latest changes. Verify each layer independently and then verify the complete user journey.

