* Browser-console inspection.
* Production smoke tests, if authorized and accessible.

Record the actual command or test procedure, its result, and any limitation.

Distinguish clearly between:

* PASS — executed and passed.
* FAIL — executed and failed.
* BLOCKED — could not execute because of an identified dependency or access restriction.
* NOT TESTED — not executed.
* NOT APPLICABLE — the feature does not exist or the test does not apply.

Do not report a test as passed because you reviewed the source code.

Do not claim 100% coverage unless measured and supported by the testing tools.

Do not fabricate screenshots, logs, test results, database responses, deployment identifiers, or browser observations.

