25. FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The project is ready to be reported as verified only when the applicable requirements below have been tested.

Routing and navigation

* Every discovered intended route has a documented status.
* All major pages render correctly.
* Internal links lead to the correct destinations.
* Redirects behave as specified.
* Direct navigation and refresh work.
* Unknown routes show the intended not-found experience.
* No unexplained redirect loops remain.

Frontend

* Major pages render at supported viewport sizes.
* Interactive controls perform their intended actions.
* Forms validate and submit correctly.
* Loading, empty, success, and error states behave correctly.
* No critical runtime errors remain in the tested journeys.
* No major page relies on fake success or placeholder data where real functionality is required.

Integration

* Critical API requests use the correct endpoints and payloads.
* Authentication and authorization are enforced.
* Database reads and writes are verified.
* UI state reflects persisted changes.
* Important failure and recovery paths work.

Property workflows

* Supported import methods use compatible contracts.
* Source information and provenance are preserved appropriately.
* Validation compares facts against available source evidence.
* Missing and conflicting facts are reported rather than fabricated.
* Reimports respect manual edits and approved versions.
* Enrichment and rewriting require explicit user action.
* Generated descriptions are independently validated.
* Approval and publishing gates are enforced.
* Background job failures are visible and recoverable.

Build and deployment

* The production build completes.
* Production configuration is correct.
* Direct route handling is verified.
* The running frontend and intended source revision are connected by evidence where deployment access permits.
* Stale UI and caching issues are investigated rather than assumed away.
* Any unverified production claim is explicitly identified.

Regression and reporting

* Critical defects have regression tests where feasible.
* Tests have actual results.
* Remaining blockers are documented.
* No test results are fabricated.
* No unapproved destructive changes have occurred.

Do not declare the application completely verified while any P0 or P1 defect remains unresolved. If an external dependency prevents completion, explain exactly what remains blocked and what evidence would be needed to finish verification.

